  <p>{{#if beta}}{{brandName}} is in beta: its features and prices may change while it is. {{/if}}{{brandName}} is offered “as is” and “as available.” It’s a small service, and it may change, break or go down, including when X changes or limits its API. We may add, change or remove features, and update these Terms; if we make material changes we’ll update the effective date and, where appropriate, tell you. Using {{brandName}} after a change means you accept the updated Terms.</p>

  <h2 class="section">8. Ending</h2>
  <p>You can stop at any time: delete your account in Settings (it revokes {{brandName}}’s access on X and deletes your data, as the Privacy Policy describes; a prepaid balance isn’t refunded), or revoke {{brandName}}’s access in your X settings. We may suspend or end your access if you break these Terms, or to protect the service or others.</p>

  <h2 class="section">9. Disclaimers and limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>To the fullest extent the law allows, {{brandName}} and {{legal.entity}} disclaim all warranties, express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. We aren’t liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential or punitive damages, or for lost data, profits or goodwill, arising from your use of {{brandName}}. Our total liability for any claim about {{brandName}} is limited to the greater of what you paid us in the twelve months before the claim or US $100. Some places don’t allow these limits, so parts of this section may not apply to you.</p>

  <h2 class="section">10. Governing law</h2>
  <p>These Terms are governed by the laws of {{#if legal.jurisdiction}}{{legal.jurisdiction}}{{else}}the place where {{legal.entity}} is established{{/if}}, without regard to its conflict-of-laws rules. Disputes go to the courts there, unless the law where you live says otherwise.</p>

